spec: S29-30, S29-31

`settings list | get | set | reset` and `devices list | rename | forget` (CMD-23) for their own
Member @kim (profile `kim`, removed again at the end), whose Web, iPhone and iPad `setup.sh`
makes the way the clients do (the CLI never makes a Device). Without `--device`, a device setting
shows its All devices value; `--device NAME` (an id, else a name, case-insensitively) resolves for
that Device. A device setting needs `--all-devices` or `--device`, a user setting neither. Every
exit path: 1 (missing or wrong flag, unknown key, bad value, low contrast, Display name reset), 2
(unknown Device or Vault), 5 (Web renamed or forgotten, a forgotten Device written), 6
(unreachable). Merged stdout+stderr; last-seen ages are `[..]`.

```console
$ sh setup.sh
profile "kim" saved → [..]/config.toml
Kim has Web, an iPhone and an iPad

$ annotary -p kim settings list
display_name	Kim	user	user
appearance	system	default	device
highlight_light	yellow	default	device
highlight_dark	yellow	default	device
text_size	100	default	device
show_resolved	hidden	default	user
default_vault	any	default	user
keyboard_shortcuts	on	default	device
send_key	enter	default	device
times	relative	default	user
clock	system	default	user

$ ANNOTARY_TTY=1 NO_COLOR=1 annotary -p kim settings
KEY                 VALUE     SOURCE   KIND
display_name        Kim       user     user
appearance          system    default  device
highlight_light     yellow    default  device
highlight_dark      yellow    default  device
text_size           100       default  device
show_resolved       hidden    default  user
default_vault       any       default  user
keyboard_shortcuts  on        default  device
send_key            enter     default  device
times               relative  default  user
clock               system    default  user

$ annotary -p kim settings list --json key,value,label,group
[{"key":"display_name","value":"Kim","label":"Display name","group":"profile"},{"key":"appearance","value":"system","label":"Appearance","group":"appearance"},{"key":"highlight_light","value":"yellow","label":"Highlight, light","group":"appearance"},{"key":"highlight_dark","value":"yellow","label":"Highlight, dark","group":"appearance"},{"key":"text_size","value":100,"label":"Text size","group":"appearance"},{"key":"show_resolved","value":"hidden","label":"Resolved Threads","group":"threads"},{"key":"default_vault","value":"any","label":"Default Vault","group":"documents"},{"key":"keyboard_shortcuts","value":"on","label":"Keyboard shortcuts","group":"keyboard"},{"key":"send_key","value":"enter","label":"Send key for replies","group":"keyboard"},{"key":"times","value":"relative","label":"Times shown as","group":"date-and-time"},{"key":"clock","value":"system","label":"Clock","group":"date-and-time"}]

$ annotary -p kim devices list
web	web	Web	[..]
01K9PH0NE00000000000000001	iphone	iPhone 17	[..]
01K9PAD0000000000000000002	ipad	iPad Pro	[..]

$ ANNOTARY_TTY=1 NO_COLOR=1 annotary -p kim devices
ID                          KIND    NAME       LAST SEEN
web                         web     Web        [..]
01K9PH0NE00000000000000001  iphone  iPhone 17  [..]
01K9PAD0000000000000000002  ipad    iPad Pro   [..]

$ annotary -p kim devices list --json id,kind,name
[{"id":"web","kind":"web","name":"Web"},{"id":"01K9PH0NE00000000000000001","kind":"iphone","name":"iPhone 17"},{"id":"01K9PAD0000000000000000002","kind":"ipad","name":"iPad Pro"}]

$ annotary -p kim settings set appearance dark
? 1
error: appearance is a device setting: say --all-devices or --device NAME — `annotary devices list` shows your Devices

$ annotary -p kim settings set times absolute --device web
? 1
error: times is a user setting, the same on every Device: drop --device — annotary settings set times VALUE

$ annotary -p kim settings set nope 1
? 1
error: no setting "nope" — GET /api/v1/me/settings/catalog lists them (`annotary settings list`)

$ annotary -p kim settings set appearance purple --all-devices
? 1
error: appearance: "purple" is not one of system, light, dark

$ annotary -p kim settings set highlight_dark "#222222" --all-devices
? 1
error: highlight_dark: text on that color has a contrast of [..]:1, below 4.5:1 — pick a lighter color for light pages, a brighter one for dark pages

$ annotary -p kim settings set appearance dark --device toaster
? 2
error: no Device toaster — name one by its id or its name (`annotary devices list --all`)
  web  Web
  01K9PH0NE00000000000000001  iPhone 17
  01K9PAD0000000000000000002  iPad Pro

$ annotary -p kim settings get nope
? 1
error: no setting "nope" — `annotary settings list` shows them

$ annotary -p kim settings set text_size 130% --all-devices
text_size	130	all	device

$ annotary -p kim settings set text_size 130 --all-devices
text_size unchanged
text_size	130	all	device

$ annotary -p kim settings set appearance light --device Web
appearance	light	device	device

$ annotary -p kim settings get appearance
appearance	system	default	device

$ ANNOTARY_TTY=1 NO_COLOR=1 annotary -p kim settings get appearance --device web
appearance  light  device  device

$ annotary -p kim settings get appearance --device web --json
{"key":"appearance","value":"light","source":"device","kind":"device"}

$ annotary -p kim settings list --device "iphone 17" --json key,value,source,device
[{"key":"display_name","value":"Kim","source":"user"},{"key":"appearance","value":"system","source":"default","device":"01K9PH0NE00000000000000001"},{"key":"highlight_light","value":"yellow","source":"default","device":"01K9PH0NE00000000000000001"},{"key":"highlight_dark","value":"yellow","source":"default","device":"01K9PH0NE00000000000000001"},{"key":"text_size","value":130,"source":"all","device":"01K9PH0NE00000000000000001"},{"key":"show_resolved","value":"hidden","source":"default"},{"key":"default_vault","value":"any","source":"default"},{"key":"keyboard_shortcuts","value":"on","source":"default","device":"01K9PH0NE00000000000000001"},{"key":"send_key","value":"enter","source":"default","device":"01K9PH0NE00000000000000001"},{"key":"times","value":"relative","source":"default"},{"key":"clock","value":"system","source":"default"}]

$ annotary -p kim settings set default_vault notes
default_vault	notes	user	user

$ annotary -p kim settings set default_vault nowhere
? 2
error: no Vault nowhere — name one you can read (notes) or `any`

$ annotary -p kim settings set times absolute --json
{"key":"times","value":"absolute","source":"user","kind":"user","changed":true}

$ ANNOTARY_TTY=1 NO_COLOR=1 annotary -p kim settings set times absolute
times unchanged
times  absolute  user  user

$ annotary -p kim settings reset appearance
? 1
error: appearance is a device setting: say --all-devices or --device NAME — `annotary devices list` shows your Devices

$ annotary -p kim settings reset appearance --device web
appearance	system	default	device

$ ANNOTARY_TTY=1 NO_COLOR=1 annotary -p kim settings reset times
times  relative  default  user

$ annotary -p kim settings reset default_vault --json
{"key":"default_vault","value":"any","source":"default","kind":"user","changed":true}

$ annotary -p kim settings reset display_name
? 1
error: display_name: a display name has no default

$ annotary -p kim devices rename "ipad pro" "Kim's iPad"
01K9PAD0000000000000000002	ipad	Kim's iPad	[..]

$ ANNOTARY_TTY=1 NO_COLOR=1 annotary -p kim devices rename 01K9PH0NE00000000000000001 "Kim's iPhone"
01K9PH0NE00000000000000001  iphone  Kim's iPhone  [..]

$ annotary -p kim devices rename web Browser
? 5
error: Web stands for every browser: it can't be renamed or forgotten — signing out of browsers is what Sign out does

$ annotary -p kim devices rename toaster x
? 2
error: no Device toaster — name one by its id or its name (`annotary devices list --all`)
  web  Web
  01K9PH0NE00000000000000001  Kim's iPhone
  01K9PAD0000000000000000002  Kim's iPad

$ annotary -p kim devices forget Web
? 5
error: Web stands for every browser: it can't be renamed or forgotten — signing out of browsers is what Sign out does

$ annotary -p kim devices forget "kim's ipad"
01K9PAD0000000000000000002	Kim's iPad	forgotten	1 Token revoked	0 sessions ended

$ ANNOTARY_TTY=1 NO_COLOR=1 annotary -p kim devices forget "Kim's iPad"
Device 01K9PAD0000000000000000002 was already forgotten
01K9PAD0000000000000000002  Kim's iPad  forgotten  0 Tokens revoked  0 sessions ended

$ annotary -p kim devices forget "Kim's iPhone" --json
{"id":"01K9PH0NE00000000000000001","name":"Kim's iPhone","forgotten":true,"tokens_revoked":1,"sessions_ended":0}

$ annotary -p kim devices list
web	web	Web	[..]

$ annotary -p kim devices list --all
web	web	Web	[..]
01K9PH0NE00000000000000001	iphone	Kim's iPhone (forgotten)	[..]
01K9PAD0000000000000000002	ipad	Kim's iPad (forgotten)	[..]

$ annotary -p kim settings set appearance dark --device "Kim's iPad"
? 5
error: Device 01K9PAD0000000000000000002 was forgotten — a forgotten Device id is never used again: make a new one

$ annotary -p rowan token list --member kim --all --json name,status
[{"name":"member add","status":"active"},{"name":"iphone","status":"revoked"},{"name":"ipad","status":"revoked"}]

$ annotary -p down settings list
? 6
error: server at http://127.0.0.1:1 not reachable — run `annotary serve` or `annotary daemon install`

$ annotary -p down devices list
? 6
error: server at http://127.0.0.1:1 not reachable — run `annotary serve` or `annotary daemon install`

$ annotary -p rowan -q profile remove kim
profile "kim" removed → [..]/config.toml

```
